ttps://github.com/tannerdanger/sorting_algorithm_analysis","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Java","description":"The purpose of this study was to compare the run-times of common sorting algorithms on two separate data structures, with 4 different data sizes. This assignment took a little bit of trial and error. The first few times I ran my code I noticed a few runtimes seemed to be much higher than it should have been. I ran through my algorithms line by line and eliminated a few loops and lines of code that caused an extra N to the runtime. Upon adjusting my code, I found my runtimes all were more consistent, and much closer to the average runtime. ","topics":[],"score":189951,"global_rank":356234},{"name":"PerrySong/FirebaseAuthDemo","owner":"PerrySong","html_url":"https://github.com/PerrySong/FirebaseAuthDemo","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Java","description":null,"topics":[],"score":189951,"global_rank":356247},{"name":"aganse/MultiRegressLines","owner":"aganse","html_url":"https://github.com/aganse/MultiRegressLines","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Java","description":"MultiRegressLines runs multiple-line (up to three) segment regression on a dataset of X,Y data.  This Java version of my code has some remaining math issues - till those are fixed please use the Matlab version for actual analysis (MultiRegressLines.matlab).  For both, my linked webpage explains this topic of \"multi-phase linear regression\".","topics":[],"score":189945,"global_rank":356253},{"name":"aganse/SpheRayDemo","owner":"aganse","html_url":"https://github.com/aganse/SpheRayDemo","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Java","description":"SpheRayDemo is a \"spherical raytrace demonstration\" of modeling raytraced ion acoustic waves propagating in the Sun.  See my webpage on helioseismology for more.  Bonus: this app's plots look like Spirograph art!","topics":[],"score":189945,"global_rank":356254},{"